# KNOWN idiom debt, one site per line. This file only ever
# SHRINKS: no tool path adds to it. A finding is fixed in the
# code, or annotated `// LICENSED I<n>: reason` at the site —
# a `native:` finding honours a license under its PREDECESSOR
# code too (NATIVE_PREDECESSOR, tools/idioms.py), so a site a
# human already reviewed under the retired regex is not
# re-litigated the day the rule that replaced it starts
# enforcing on its own. What sits below has no license under
# either code: a `native:` site is either a RULE MATCHING
# ITS OWN QUOTE PATTERN (compiler/idioms.av's declarations —
# a structural artifact, since a pattern necessarily spells
# the shape it detects) or genuinely unreviewed debt.
# `make idioms-accept` prunes what is gone. Burn it down.
